<Project>
  <!-- The one place in the repository where a version number is written, as docs/decisions/0004-versioning-and-release-policy.md
       records. It sits at the repository root rather than inside a stack because both stacks report it: the service and
       the client ship together, and a bug report that named two numbers would be describing one product twice. Each
       stack's own Directory.Build.props imports this file, so the number reaches every assembly without either stack
       owning it.

       It names the *next* release rather than the last one, so every build from main is a preview of what the next tag
       will carry, and raising it is a reviewed diff rather than a tag typed from a shell.

       Continuous integration contributes the two properties this file does not carry, and nothing else. VersionSuffix
       turns a build into a prerelease of this same version — `nightly.<run number>` — and SourceRevisionId appends
       `+<sha>` to InformationalVersion, which is what lets a running process name the commit it was built from. Neither
       is set here, and neither has to be: a build inside a worktree resolves the revision through the SDK's source-link
       support, and a build without one carries whatever its caller passed. No Git *tag* is read at any point, so a
       shallow clone stamps the same version as a full one and the silent 0.0.0 that a tag-derived scheme produces
       cannot occur.

       AssemblyVersion and FileVersion are stated rather than left to the SDK because they must never carry the
       prerelease suffix: both are numeric-only fields, and a nightly and the release it previews are deliberately the
       same assembly identity. InformationalVersion is left to the SDK, which is what composes VersionPrefix,
       VersionSuffix, and SourceRevisionId into the single string the runtime reports. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <VersionPrefix>0.8.0</VersionPrefix>
    <AssemblyVersion>$(VersionPrefix)</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>$(VersionPrefix)</FileVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
